title Detailed Design - Before Pattern Implementation (Monolithic / Violates OCP)

class AllocationController <<Control>> {
    - validator : ConflictValidator
    - rankingMode : String
    + allocateLessonSlot(lessonId : String, teacherId : String, studioId : String, slot : TimeSlot) : Boolean
    + rankCandidates(candidates : List<Teacher>, slot : TimeSlot, mode : String) : List<Teacher>
}

class Teacher <<Entity>> {
    - weeklyHoursTarget : float
    - runningWeeklyHours : float
    + getRunningWeeklyHours() : float
    + getRunningMonthlyHours() : float
}

AllocationController --> "0..*" Teacher : directly sorts >

note right of AllocationController::rankCandidates
  <b>Monolithic Conditional Logic:</b>
  <code>
  if (mode.equals("WORKLOAD_DEFICIT")) {
      // Inline sort by (40.0 - runningWeeklyHours)
  } else if (mode.equals("PREFERENCE_MATCH")) {
      // Inline sort by teacher day/clustering preference
  } else if (mode.equals("SENIORITY")) {
      // Requires modifying AllocationController!
  }
  </code>
  <b>Critical Design Flaws:</b>
  * Violates Open-Closed Principle (OCP): Adding new ranking rules requires editing and recompiling core controller.
  * Violates Single Responsibility Principle (SRP): Orchestration controller bloated with mathematical ranking logic.
  * Tightly coupled to sorting internals, impeding isolated unit testing.
end note

@enduml
